The getter is already a single delegating call with no redundant work, so the only safe drop-in is the identical body; any manual field access would require internals not visible here and risks behavioural divergence.

```cpp
    FIT_UINT16 GetProcessingInterval(void) const
    {
        return GetFieldUINT16Value(0, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```